      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CHOOSE Go when: microservices, CLIs, network servers, concurrent workloads, teams wanting simplicity with safety.\nCHOOSE Java when: enterprise apps, existing JVM ecosystem, complex business logic, long-running services with mature GC tuning.\nCHOOSE Rust when: systems programming, WebAssembly, game engines, real-time systems, or when C++ safety is a concern.\nCHOOSE C++ when: legacy codebase, game dev with full control, embedded systems, libraries requiring ABI stability.\nCHOOSE Node.js when: JavaScript team, I/O-heavy web APIs, SSR, tooling, and when single-thread simplicity is acceptable.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CHOOSE Go when: microservices, CLIs, network servers, concurrent workloads, teams wanting simplicity with safety.\nCHOOSE Java when: enterprise apps, existing JVM ecosystem, complex business logic, long-running services with mature GC tuning.\nCHOOSE Rust when: systems programming, WebAssembly, game engines, real-time systems, or when C++ safety is a concern.\nCHOOSE C++ when: legacy codebase, game dev with full control, embedded systems, libraries requiring ABI stability.\nCHOOSE Node.js when: JavaScript team, I/O-heavy web APIs, SSR, tooling, and when single-thread simplicity is acceptable.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
